cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "agent-builder-charter: an executable, runtime-enforced governance manifest for AI agents"
message: "If you use this project or build on it, please cite it and keep attribution."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pahwa
    given-names: Ayan
    website: "https://codensolder.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/iayanpahwa/agent-builder-charter"
url: "https://codensolder.com"
abstract: >
  CHARTER is a per-agent governance manifest (charter.yaml) that lists the only
  things an agent may do: model, tools, budget, network egress, credentials,
  approvals, data handling, and evals. A runtime loader reads the charter and is
  the only door: anything not on the file is blocked. The project ships a
  framework-neutral core plus builders that turn a charter into an enforced,
  runnable agent (the first builder runs agents headless via claude -p).
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - agent-governance
  - llm-safety
  - claude-code
  - guardrails
license: Apache-2.0
